<% content_for :title, "Discount Calculator — whizwheel" %>

<%#
  Discount calculator page (spec issue #254, DESIGN.md BLEND) — a single-formula, multi-input
  calculator in the shape proven by Tip/Percentage: an original price and a discount, computing
  the final (sale) price and the amount saved. A required `mode` picker selects HOW the discount
  is expressed — a percent off, or a fixed dollar amount off — and the form shows only the one
  discount field that mode uses. The form posts over Turbo and re-renders the #result region in
  place; it works WITHOUT JS — the server validates exactly the selected mode's required field
  and re-renders the result fragment. The discount_controller is pure polish: it reveals only the
  active mode's discount field (disabling the other so it's never posted) and lifts the active row.

  Mode-picker choice (DESIGN.md §4 "Mode picker"): TWO modes (N=2), but both labels read as
  multi-word ("Percent off" / "Fixed amount off"). The §4 rule reserves the segmented control for
  N ≤ 3 with SHORT labels; a multi-word label routes to the SELECTABLE OPTION LIST (.mode-option),
  which also gives each mode a helper line naming what it does. It stays a native radio
  <fieldset>/<legend> posting a single-select inputs[mode].

  Layout per DESIGN.md §3 — an input column + a results panel (≈380px 1fr), collapsing to one
  column on mobile. Spacing scale ("targets not minimums"):
    • stacked fields → space-y-5
    • major blocks within the card (mode → fields → submit) → mt-8 (Section tier)
    • column gutters / card padding → gap-8 / p-7–p-8 (Layout tier)
%>

<header class="max-w-2xl">
  <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-accent">Financial</p>
  <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.035em] text-ink">Discount Calculator</h1>
  <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
    Apply a discount to a price and see the
    <span class="font-semibold text-ink">final sale price</span> and exactly
    <span class="font-semibold text-ink">how much you saved</span>. Express the discount as a
    percent off or a fixed dollar amount off. Every figure is computed server-side.
  </p>
</header>

<div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[380px_1fr]">
  <%# ── Input column ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── %>
  <section class="rounded-[18px] border border-border bg-surface p-7 shadow-[0_10px_34px_rgba(150,110,80,0.12)] sm:p-8">
    <%= form_with url: "/calculators/discount", scope: :inputs, method: :post,
          data: { controller: "discount" } do |f| %>

      <%# Mode picker — selectable option list (.mode-option), per DESIGN.md §4: two multi-word
          modes → one bordered, divided container of full-width rows, NOT a segmented control
          (reserved for N ≤ 3 short labels). The accessible control is a native radio
          <fieldset>/<legend> posting inputs[mode]; each radio is visually-hidden (peer sr-only)
          and paired to a styled <label for>. The active row is painted with no JS via
          peer:checked, and the .mode-option::before radio glyph is the non-colour active cue
          (DESIGN.md §6). Each row names HOW the discount is expressed (bold label) + a helper. %>
      <fieldset>
        <legend class="text-xs font-bold text-label">Discount type</legend>
        <div class="mt-3 overflow-hidden rounded-[13px] border border-border-input divide-y divide-rule">
          <% discount_modes.each_with_index do |m, i| %>
            <div>
              <%= f.radio_button :mode, m[:value],
                    checked: i.zero?,
                    class: "peer sr-only",
                    data: { discount_target: "modeInput", action: "discount#select" } %>
              <%= f.label :mode, value: m[:value],
                    class: "mode-option",
                    data: { discount_target: "modeOption", mode: m[:value] } do %>
                <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink"><%= m[:label] %></span>
                <span class="text-xs text-muted"><%= m[:helper] %></span>
              <% end %>
            </div>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </fieldset>

      <%# Fields. Stacked tier: space-y-5 down the column (DESIGN.md §3). The original price is
          given in every mode; the two discount fields each declare the mode they serve via
          data-discount-mode, and Stimulus shows only the active mode's field and disables the
          other so it's never posted (the no-JS baseline shows both — the server reads only the
          mode's required field). Each input carries its $/% affix on the Affix tier (gap-2). %>
      <div class="mt-8 space-y-5">
        <%# Original price — given in both modes. $ leading affix. %>
        <div>
          <%= f.label :original_price, "Original price", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_original_price" %>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">$</span>
            <%= f.number_field :original_price, id: "inputs_original_price", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal",
                  min: "0", placeholder: "0.00", class: "field-input" %>
          </div>
        </div>

        <%# Percent off — used by the `percent` mode only. % trailing affix. %>
        <div data-discount-target="field" data-discount-mode="percent">
          <%= f.label :percent_off, "Percent off", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_percent_off" %>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <%= f.number_field :percent_off, id: "inputs_percent_off", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal",
                  min: "0", max: "100", placeholder: "0", class: "field-input" %>
            <span class="text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">%</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <%# Amount off — used by the `fixed` mode only. $ leading affix. %>
        <div data-discount-target="field" data-discount-mode="fixed">
          <%= f.label :amount_off, "Amount off", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_amount_off" %>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">$</span>
            <%= f.number_field :amount_off, id: "inputs_amount_off", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal",
                  min: "0", placeholder: "0.00", class: "field-input" %>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <%# Submit — Section tier above; primary coral button (DESIGN.md §4). %>
      <%= f.submit "Calculate",
            class: "mt-8 w-full cursor-pointer rounded-[13px] bg-primary px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-surface shadow-sm transition-opacity hover:opacity-90 focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent" %>
    <% end %>
  </section>

  <%# ── Results panel (the Turbo target) ─────────────────────────────────── %>
  <section id="result" aria-live="polite">
    <%= render "calculators/result", calc: nil %>
  </section>
</div>
